  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Standard electrode potential is a measurement of the potential for equilibrium. There is a potential difference between the electrode and the electrolyte called the potential of the electrode. When unity is the concentrations of all the species involved in a semi-cell, the electrode potential is known as the standard electrode potential.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0126_eb7822229fc4.png\" style=\"width: 262px; height: 108px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>3</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>3</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>036</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>44</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>772</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mtext>cell&#160;</mtext><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>233</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></msub><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>96</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>233</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi></math></p>"
  }
